          "title": "Prompting Mental Model",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. What a Prompt Does",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Prompt = the ==only input== that steers a **frozen** model",
                "Model predicts ==next tokens== from your text",
                "Clearer context → better output"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Zero-shot vs Few-shot",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "",
                "Zero-shot",
                "Few-shot"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Prompt",
                  "instruction only",
                  "2-5 worked input→output examples"
                ],
                [
                  "Good for",
                  "summarise, translate",
                  "format or style to copy"
                ],
                [
                  "Weights",
                  "unchanged",
                  "unchanged (in-context learning)"
                ]
              ],
              "frame": "dashed"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Prompt Anatomy",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "chain",
              "spec": {
                "steps": [
                  {
                    "text": "Role / system",
                    "ink": "blue"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Task instruction",
                    "ink": "green"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Context / data",
                    "ink": "orange"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Examples",
                    "ink": "purple"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Output format",
                    "ink": "pink"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "4. Not Deterministic",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Test sets, not one try",
              "text": "Same prompt can give ==different outputs==. Test on a **set of cases**."
            },
            {
              "type": "sidebox",
              "title": "Interview Point",
              "items": [
                "**Zero-shot vs few-shot?** No examples vs 2-5; no weights change",
                "**Is a prompt deterministic?** No; test on a case set"
              ],
              "ink": "orange"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Core Workflow: Zero-Shot to Few-Shot",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 1,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Core Workflow: Zero-Shot to Few-Shot",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Zero-Shot First",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Specific ==instruction==, audience, output format",
                "Add examples only if output ==misses the target=="
              ],
              "style": "check",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Choosing Examples",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Cover ==edge cases== and label variety",
                "Keep every example in the ==same format==",
                "Skewed labels bias the answer toward the majority",
                "The ==last example== pulls hardest: recency bias"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Delimit Sections",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "text",
              "lines": [
                "### Instruction",
                "Label the review's sentiment.",
                "### Examples",
                "<example>great -> pos</example>",
                "### Data",
                "<review>{text}</review>"
              ],
              "note": "tags or ### keep instructions, examples and data apart"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "4. Iterate Loop",
              "ink": "orange"
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "flow",
              "spec": {
                "nodes": [
                  {
                    "text": "Write prompt",
                    "ink": "green"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Run",
                    "sub": "5-10 inputs",
                    "ink": "blue"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Inspect failures",
                    "ink": "red"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Change one thing",
                    "ink": "orange"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Rerun",
                    "ink": "purple"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Change one thing",
              "text": "Two edits at once and you cannot tell which one helped."
            },
            {
              "type": "sidebox",
              "title": "Interview Point",
              "items": [
                "**Why start zero-shot?** Cheapest; add examples only when output misses.",
                "**What is recency bias?** The last example sways the answer.",
                "**Why delimit?** The model cannot tell instructions from data."
              ],
              "ink": "purple"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "System Prompts and Chain-of-Thought",
