    {
      "title": "Structured Output and Sampling Controls",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 3,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Structured Output and Sampling Controls",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Structured Output",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Ask for ==JSON== matching a schema, plus one example",
                "Prefer the API's **JSON mode**, schema-constrained or tool-call output",
                "{red:Never trust raw text}: parse, validate, retry or repair"
              ],
              "style": "check"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "python",
              "lines": [
                "import json",
                "text = '{\"label\": \"spam\"}'",
                "try:",
                "    data = json.loads(text)",
                "    assert data[\"label\"] in {\"spam\", \"ham\"}",
                "    print(\"ok\", data[\"label\"])",
                "except (ValueError, KeyError, AssertionError):",
                "    print(\"retry\")"
              ],
              "note": "parse, then schema check"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "output",
              "lines": [
                "ok spam"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Sampling Controls",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Task",
                "Temperature"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Extraction, classification, code",
                  "0 to ~0.3"
                ],
                [
                  "Brainstorming, creative writing",
                  "0.7 to 1"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "==Temperature== scales randomness",
                "==Top-p== samples only the smallest token set whose probability sums to p",
                "{orange:Rule}: tune temperature **or** top-p, not both"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Limits and Interview Point",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Low temperature is not a guarantee",
              "text": "It only makes output more ==repeatable==. It is not deterministic and can still be **confidently wrong**."
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "**Why validate JSON output?** Raw text can be malformed or off-schema.",
                "**Does temperature 0 make answers correct?** No, only more repeatable."
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Prompt Injection and Common Mistakes",
      "role": "outline",
